WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.170
Here's how to give a game its own profile,

2
00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.670
so PadForge switches to it when the game comes to the front.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:08.850
You're hearing a generated voice.

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.910
Set PadForge up the way you want for the game.

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.350
Then open the Profiles page, and click Save As.

6
00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:20.682
Name it after the game.

7
00:00:21.092 --> 00:00:23.102
Click Browse, and pick the game's program.

8
00:00:23.652 --> 00:00:25.882
Here, Character Map stands in for a game.

9
00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.982
Then click Save.

10
00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:32.059
Tick Auto-Switch Profiles Based on Foreground Application.

11
00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:35.159
The Foreground line shows the program in front.

12
00:00:37.168 --> 00:00:40.838
Bring the game to the front, and PadForge loads its profile.

13
00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:43.538
The program's name lights up while it matches.

14
00:00:45.508 --> 00:00:49.218
Switch to anything else, and PadForge goes back to Default.

15
00:00:50.128 --> 00:00:52.738
Changes you make save into whichever profile is loaded.

16
00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:57.843
Find more guides at padforge.org.
